---
import Admin from '../../layouts/Admin.astro';
---
<Admin title="Overview" active="home">

  <h1 class="adm-h1">Admin</h1>
  <p class="adm-lede">
    Update the website without touching GitHub. Everything you change here goes
    live on jmcengg.com.
  </p>

  <div class="adm-grid">

    <div class="adm-card soon">
      <span class="adm-tag">Being built</span>
      <h2>Photos</h2>
      <p>
        Upload photographs of finished tools, the shop floor and work in progress.
        They appear in the Our Work section on the homepage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="adm-card soon">
      <span class="adm-tag">Being built</span>
      <h2>Writing</h2>
      <p>
        Write and publish articles. These are what bring engineers to the site
        from a search, so they stay part of the site rather than loading later.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="adm-note">
    <p>
      <b>Who can get in.</b> Signing in with a Microsoft account is not enough on
      its own — an account needs a role before any of this is reachable, and
      roles are handed out by invitation from the Azure portal. Someone who
      finds this address and signs in without an invitation is refused.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">
      <b>The two roles.</b> <code>editor</code> can add photos and write
      articles. <code>admin</code> can do that and invite other people. To add
      a colleague, see <code>docs/admin-panel.md</code> in the repository, or
      ask whoever set this up.
    </p>
  </div>

</Admin>
